  "notes": "From the pool-court views (00-04, 06): the pool runs across the lot between the two houses, the main house's glazed ground floor on one long side and the yellow guest block's long face (one horizontal window, one slit) on the other, a pale ledge along the yellow wall and a paved strip along the glass; a floating stair of cantilevered treads on the white west end wall climbing to the guest block's roof; palms in pots and sunbeds on gravel beside the guest block at the pool's east end, a timber screen behind; on the guest roof a sunken U of yellow benches with white cushions and grasses behind, under a concrete canopy on a steel frame that runs out east over the palms; the main house's upper storey yellow with three tall narrow windows between a grey concrete band and a grey parapet. This pass: Izamal yellow drawn as yellow (was ochre); the pool widened to fill the court and ended at the guest block's east corner as the photographs show; the stair re-stepped to reach the guest roof at its face; the roof lounge given its yellow U bench, cushions, table and grasses; the palms drawn as palms in dark pots; the main house's parapet band deepened and its roof drawn pale; the party walls kept only round the court (the main house fills the lot's width). Orientation guessed: street to the south, rear garden to the north. The street front, the rear garden, the ends of the main house and the lot's exact dimensions were not shown and are guessed from a typical narrow Yucatecan lot; the pool's entry steps and the stair's railing are too fine to draw."
